{title: Face to Face}
{artist: Carrie E. Breck / Grant C. Tullar}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Face to face with [D]Christ, my [A]Saviour
[E7]Face to face, what will it [A]be
When with [A]rapture I be[D]hold Him
[E7]Jesus Christ who died for [A]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]Face to face I [D]shall be[A]hold Him
[E7]Far beyond the starry [A]sky
[A]Face to face in [D]all His [A]glory
I shall [E7]see Him by and [A]by
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Only faintly [D]now I [A]see Him
[E7]With the darkened veil be[A]tween
But a [A]blessed day is [D]coming
[E7]When His glory shall be [A]seen
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]What rejoicing [D]in His [A]presence
[E7]When are banished grief and [A]pain
When the [A]crooked ways are [D]straightened
And the [E7]dark things shall be [A]plain
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[A]Face to face, oh, [D]blissful [A]moment
[E7]Face to face, to see and [A]know
[A]Face to face with [D]my Re[A]deemer
[E7]Jesus Christ who loves me [A]so
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
